  "question": {
    "text": "If the distance of point <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the line <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> measured parallel to the plane <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> is <math><mi>k</mi></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4573",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/c01816aa-e73e-4988-9860-19d14888b6ff.png\" style=\"width:3.43333in;height:1.60694in\" /><br />Coordinates of the point <math><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1,3</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2,4</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math> is perpendicular to the normal vector of the plane,<br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math><br />Normal vector <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math><br />Hence, <math><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></math><br />So, the coordinates of the point <math><mi>Q</mi></math> are&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>26</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>51</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4573</mn></msqrt></math>",
